		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>We introduce the new concept of an Arabic Derivational Chain Bank (CHAINBANK) to leverage the relationship between form and meaning in modeling Arabic derivational morphology. We constructed a knowledge graph network of abstract patterns and their derivational relations, and aligned it with the lemmas of the CAMELMORPH morphological analyzer database. This process produced chains of derived words&apos; lemmas linked to their corresponding lemma bases through derivational relations, encompassing 23,333 derivational connections. The CHAINBANK is publicly available. 1</p>
			</abstract>
